; ============================================================
; TITLE:    Lesson Transcript
; CATEGORY: Files & Data
; LEVEL:    Beginner
; TAGS:     dribble, nodribble, files, times tables
; SUMMARY:  Uses DRIBBLE to keep a copy of everything printed during a short times-table session, then reads the copy back.
; ============================================================
;
; WHAT IT DOES
;   DRIBBLE "/projects/transcript.txt starts a recording: from then on
;   everything that appears in the command center is also written into
;   that file. The program prints a times table and asks two questions
;   while recording, stops with NODRIBBLE, and then reads the
;   transcript to count its lines and print it back with line numbers.
;
; HOW TO USE
;   Press Run and answer the two sums. Afterwards open
;   /projects/transcript.txt in the file panel. Teachers can use DRIBBLE
;   to keep a record of a whole lesson at the keyboard.
;
; CONCEPTS YOU WILL LEARN
;   * DRIBBLE and NODRIBBLE
;   * the difference between a transcript, which copies the screen,
;     and SETWRITE, which sends output only to the file
;
; THINGS TO TRY
;   * Dribble your own work in the command center for a few minutes
;   * Make the session ask five questions instead of two
; ============================================================

make "transcript "/projects/transcript.txt

to table :n
  for [i 1 10] [print (sentence :i "x :n "= :i * :n)]
end

to ask.sum :a :b
  print (sentence [What is] :a "x :b "?)
  localmake "reply readword
  ifelse equalp :reply :a * :b [print [Correct.]] [print (sentence [The answer is] :a * :b)]
end

to number.lines :file
  localmake "n 0
  openread :file
  setread :file
  while [not eofp] [
    make "n :n + 1
    ; READWORD keeps the line exactly as the transcript stored it.
    print (sentence :n "| | readword)
  ]
  setread []
  close :file
  output :n
end

; If an earlier run left a transcript behind, we start a fresh one.
if filep :transcript [erasefile :transcript]
dribble :transcript
print [=== Times table session ===]
table 7
ask.sum 6 7
ask.sum 8 7
print [=== End of session ===]
nodribble

print []
print [Here is what the transcript file holds:]
make "count number.lines :transcript
print (sentence [The transcript has] :count [lines.])
